var e={employee:{Kevin:{role:`IT — apprentice, year 3`,reason:`For carrying a burning waste-paper bin outside on his own initiative. The jury expressly commends the calm with which he walked past four fire extinguishers on the way.`},Chantal:{role:`Marketing & feel-good management`,reason:`For introducing the term 'intensive growth opportunity'. The number of reported cases of stress has fallen to zero since.`},Egon:{role:`Facilities Management`,reason:`For forty-one years of service without a single complaint. The jury points out that Mr Egon does not take complaints either.`},"Dr. Wichtig":{role:`Chief Executive Officer`,reason:`For visionary leadership in a challenging market environment. The award was decided unanimously by management. Management consists of Dr Wichtig.`},Gabi:{role:`Reception & Switchboard`,reason:`For putting through 1,400 calls in one month, 1,390 of them to IT. The jury praises her unwavering clarification of responsibility.`},"Frau Elster":{role:`Accounts`,reason:`For clearing up a receipt matter of €3.49 without a single gap. The work took eleven hours. The jury commends the attitude, not the balance.`},Markus:{role:`Senior VP of Synergies`,reason:`For signing a contract for a product that is at present still in the concept phase. Rollout: as soon as technically possible.`}},employeeSelf:{name:`Miller`,role:`Systems administration`,reason:`The jury asked in every department this month and got the same answer everywhere. No photograph is available; the recipient was in the server room at the time of the shoot. He was in the server room for the second appointment as well.`},employeeNone:{title:`Not awarded`,reason:`The award is being withheld this month. The jury refers to ongoing proceedings and thanks all staff for their understanding.`},feed:[{id:`feed_gala`,author:`Human Capital`,handle:`@HR_Compliance`,initials:`HR`,tone:`#f9a8d4`,text:`Regarding the repeated enquiries about the Synergy Gala: invitations are issued to staff who have proven themselves across departments. Assessment is ongoing. We ask that you refrain from individual requests.`},{id:`feed_tasse`,author:`Chantal`,handle:`@HR_FeelGood`,initials:`CH`,tone:`#f472b6`,text:`Who took my 'Good Vibes Only' mug out of the dishwasher without emptying the rest of it? The vibes are in the negative now!! 😭🧘‍♀️`},{id:`feed_wasser`,author:`Egon`,handle:`@Facility`,initials:`EG`,tone:`#94a3b8`,text:`The water in the kitchenette on the second floor is switched off. Reason: somebody tipped ground coffee straight into the sink.`},{id:`feed_kuehlschrank`,author:`Frau Elster`,handle:`@Accounts`,initials:`FE`,tone:`#a78bfa`,text:`The fridge in the kitchenette will be emptied on Friday at 16:00. Anything without a name on it will be thrown away. Anything with a name on it will be noted.`},{id:`feed_fundbuero`,author:`Gabi`,handle:`@Reception`,initials:`GA`,tone:`#38bdf8`,text:`Sitting at reception for three weeks now: two umbrellas, a charging cable and a pair of reading glasses. The one with the frogs on it still awaits a keeper.`},{id:`feed_drucker`,author:`Markus`,handle:`@Sales`,initials:`MA`,tone:`#fbbf24`,text:`To whoever it was: the third-floor printer is back on double-sided. We negotiate contracts up here, not leaflets.`},{id:`feed_backup`,author:`Dr. Wichtig`,handle:`@CEO`,initials:`DW`,tone:`#34d399`,text:`A brief thought from the lounge in Zurich: if we all had just ten per cent more courage, we would need half as many backups. Have a think about that.`},{id:`feed_rack5`,author:`Kevin`,handle:`@IT_NextGen`,initials:`KE`,tone:`#4ade80`,text:`Quick one for the room: does anyone know what the server in Rack 5 is actually for? Asking for a friend. The friend is me. It's urgent.`},{id:`feed_abkuerzung`,author:`Egon`,handle:`@Facility`,initials:`EG`,tone:`#94a3b8`,text:`The passage through to Store K3 is not a route to the canteen. It is not a short cut either. It is a store room.`},{id:`feed_obstkorb`,author:`Chantal`,handle:`@HR_FeelGood`,initials:`CH`,tone:`#f472b6`,text:`Tiny reminder about our fruit basket scheme: whoever finds a pear may keep it, but has to log it here because it counts as a benefit in kind. Entries so far: none. Pears gone missing: eleven. 🍐`},{id:`feed_telefon`,author:`Gabi`,handle:`@Reception`,initials:`GA`,tone:`#38bdf8`,text:`Somebody rang the switchboard again today to ask whether their phone was working. We were able to settle that during the call.`},{id:`feed_belege`,author:`Frau Elster`,handle:`@Accounts`,initials:`FE`,tone:`#a78bfa`,text:`I point this out once more: a receipt without a date is not a receipt. It is paper. Paper is not reimbursed.`},{id:`feed_adapter`,author:`Markus`,handle:`@Sales`,initials:`MA`,tone:`#fbbf24`,text:`URGENTLY NEED an adapter, HDMI to anything. Client meeting in twenty minutes. Straight to my mobile please, I don't follow this feed.`},{id:`feed_aufzug`,author:`Dr. Wichtig`,handle:`@CEO`,initials:`DW`,tone:`#34d399`,text:`I took the lift this morning and saw three members of staff who were not smiling. I set that down here without judgement. I am merely setting it down.`},{id:`feed_schild`,author:`Facilities Management`,handle:`@BuildingServices`,initials:`FM`,tone:`#fb923c`,text:`The label 'DO NOT SWITCH OFF' on the units in the plant room is not a recommendation. It is a label.`},{id:`feed_halgerd`,author:`H.A.L.G.E.R.D.`,handle:`@SystemMonitoring`,initials:`HD`,tone:`#22d3ee`,text:`Your average response time has improved by 12% over the current quarter. The target value has accordingly been adjusted by 15%. Congratulations.`},{id:`feed_kalk_essig`,reqStory:`path_kalk_essig`,author:`Facilities Management`,handle:`@BuildingServices`,initials:`FM`,tone:`#fb923c`,text:`Notice regarding the coffee machine on the second floor: an employee today took it upon himself to apply a cleaning product from the cleaning cupboard. Management thanks him for the initiative and asks that the result not be drunk.`},{id:`feed_kalk_ignor`,reqStory:`path_kalk_ignor`,author:`Central Purchasing`,handle:`@Procurement`,initials:`CP`,tone:`#60a5fa`,text:`Good news: the request for descaler has been taken into the 2027 procurement round. Until then, holding the button down counts as an officially signed-off interim solution. Many thanks to IT for the pragmatic attitude.`},{id:`feed_karton`,reqStory:`path_karton_kult`,author:`Facilities Management`,handle:`@BuildingServices`,initials:`FM`,tone:`#fb923c`,text:`Meetingpoint K1 has been added to the room booking system. Capacity: three standing places, no socket. The copier wrapped up inside it remains part of the furnishings until responsibility has been clarified.`},{id:`feed_licht`,reqStory:`path_licht_hart`,author:`Chantal`,handle:`@HR_FeelGood`,initials:`CH`,tone:`#f472b6`,text:`The mindfulness corner on the second floor was taken down today for 'infrastructural reasons'. I don't want to point the finger at anybody. I only want to put on record that the energy on this floor has been measurably different ever since. 🕯️`},{id:`feed_phoenix`,reqStory:`path_phoenix_storno`,author:`Internal Audit`,handle:`@Compliance`,initials:`IA`,tone:`#f87171`,text:`The recurring booking of room 'Creative 2' was released without sign-off. We ask whoever is responsible for Project Phoenix to reply, so that the matter can be allocated. Replies so far: none.`},{id:`feed_exting`,reqStory:`path_exting_lager`,author:`Fire Safety Officer`,handle:`@Safety`,initials:`FS`,tone:`#f87171`,text:`The inspection found the inventory to be out by two fire extinguishers. As both units are tested and carry a valid label, the discrepancy was booked as positive and the matter closed.`},{id:`feed_gemba`,reqStory:`path_gemba_show`,author:`Dr. Wichtig`,handle:`@CEO`,initials:`DW`,tone:`#34d399`,text:`I was down in IT today. What I saw there was world class: latency anomalies in the east cluster, in real time, on three screens at once. This is exactly the culture I mean. I have already put the east cluster team forward for the innovation prize.`},{id:`feed_wiki`,reqStory:`path_kevin_tutorial`,author:`Kevin`,handle:`@IT_NextGen`,initials:`KE`,tone:`#4ade80`,text:`Fixed a fault in the field of display technology together with my supervisor today and wrote the solution up in the new IT wiki. Article 1 of many! 💪`}],visions:[`We do not build software. We weave the digital garment of the future, in which the human being is merely a plugin.`,`A problem is only a solution nobody has invoiced yet.`,`I do not read reports. I feel figures.`,`Anyone who needs breaks has not yet found their why.`,`Failure is a gift. Wrap it up and put it on my desk. I will sell it on.`,`Our clients do not buy a product. They buy permission to belong.`,`I have no strategy. I have a direction, and it changes with the light.`,`Clocking off is a rumour that refuses to die.`,`Innovation does not arise in the budget. So we are cutting it.`,`If you lie awake at night thinking about our quarterly targets: that reassures me enormously.`,`Our hierarchy is flat. Mine is the flattest, because I am standing on top of it.`,`Data is the new oil. And as with oil, nobody asks where exactly it came from.`,`A backup is essentially a vote of no confidence in the future.`,`I delegate responsibility, but not authority. Anything else would be negligent.`,`The client is always right. From the moment he has signed, he is right in particular.`,`Work-life balance means both of them happening under the same roof.`,`We are not a business. We are a narrative with a VAT number.`,`You have to pick people up where they stand. Mostly they are standing in the way.`,`I believe in flat processes, short paths and long working days.`,`For us, sustainability means above all this: we can sustain it.`],status:[{label:`Coffee machine (IT)`,value:`Out of order`,tone:`bad`},{label:`Coffee machine (Sales)`,value:`Serviced`,tone:`good`},{label:`Main Server`,value:`Smoking slightly`,tone:`warn`},{label:`Printer (3rd floor)`,value:`Spare part from 2021`,tone:`warn`},{label:`Backup`,value:`Runs unchecked`,tone:`warn`},{label:`Guest Wi-Fi`,value:`Password: guest`,tone:`bad`},{label:`Phone system`,value:`Reachable`,tone:`good`},{label:`Fax machine (Reception)`,value:`Ready for use`,tone:`good`},{label:`Air con (server room)`,value:`Window open`,tone:`warn`},{label:`Ticket system`,value:`Available`,tone:`good`},{label:`Time system`,value:`Always available`,tone:`good`},{label:`Intranet search`,value:`Disabled`,tone:`bad`},{label:`Emergency power`,value:`Untested`,tone:`warn`},{label:`Door (server room)`,value:`Sticks`,tone:`warn`},{label:`Password policy`,value:`In force since 2019`,tone:`neutral`}],kpi:{blind:{value:`—`,text:`At the request of the division head, the figure is not being disclosed at present. The metric is of course still recorded.`},levels:[{min:7,text:`The figure lies well above target. As an immediate measure the metric has been set to 'under observation'.`},{min:4,text:`The deviation has been reported to the division head. A reply is not provided for.`},{min:1,text:`Deviation within range. No action is required at present.`},{min:0,text:`The target has been reached. To avoid raising expectations, the metric will no longer be collected.`}]},incident:[{min:10,note:`Close to a record. Management is examining whether the server room is being fully used.`},{min:5,note:`Stable. Please do not talk about it.`},{min:1,note:`Upward trend detected.`},{min:0,note:`The counter was reset this morning. As on most days.`}],dashboard:{page:{kind:`panel`,welcomeTitle:`Welcome to Q4! 🚀`,welcomeText:`Our pivot to the "AI-powered blockchain solution" was a complete success! Even though our product team is still working out what exactly that means for our core software, marketing has already collected three industry awards for it. Remember: we are agile. We promise the future and deliver it as soon as it arrives.`,facilityTitle:`Facility update`,facilityText:`The door to the main server room sticks from time to time. Egon the caretaker asks that people stop hitting it with the fire extinguisher. For now, please use the unsecured side entrance.`,employeeTitle:`🏅 Employee of the month`,feedTitle:`📌 Company feed`,visionTitle:`Vision of the day`,visionFallback:`We do not build software. We weave the digital garment of the future, in which the human being is merely a plugin.`,visionAuthor:`— Dr. Wichtig, CEO`,statusTitle:`System status`,incidentLabel:[`Days without an incident`,`in the server room:`],kpiTitle:`Metric of the day`,kpiLabel:`Open tickets`,kpiTargetLabel:`Target`,kpiTarget:`0`}},kantine:{page:{kind:`menu`,title:`Cafeteria: "The Agile Kitchen" 🥗`,dayLabel:`Weekday`,classicLabel:`Menu 1 (classic)`,veggieLabel:`Menu 2 (vegetarian)`,todayLabel:`Today`,hygieneTitle:`⚠️ HYGIENE NOTICE FROM EGON`,hygieneFallback:`The microwave in the east wing remains out of use until further notice.`,menu:[{id:`mon`,day:`Monday`,classic:{name:`Spaghetti bolognese`,note:`The pasta is soft. There is plenty of sauce.`},veggie:{name:`Lentil stew`,note:`Hearty, but barely salted. Comes with a stale roll.`}},{id:`tue`,day:`Tuesday`,classic:{name:`Currywurst and chips`,note:`The classic. Sadly the chips are no longer crisp.`},veggie:{name:`Steamed broccoli with rice`,note:`No sauce. Very healthy. Very dry.`}},{id:`wed`,day:`Wednesday`,classic:{name:`Chicken breast 'Hawaii'`,note:`Baked under pineapple and processed cheese.`},veggie:{name:`Large salad bowl`,note:`Plenty of iceberg lettuce, three grains of sweetcorn. Oil and vinegar dressing (sold out).`}},{id:`thu`,day:`Thursday`,classic:{name:`Schnitzel 'Viennese style'`,note:`The breadcrumbs come away easily. Potato salad out of a bucket.`},veggie:{name:`Potato soup`,note:`Watery, but warming.`}},{id:`fri`,day:`Friday`,classic:{name:`Fish fingers (4)`,note:`With mashed potato (from powder) and a little spinach.`},veggie:{name:`Vegetable wraps`,note:`Served cold. Heavy on the cream cheese.`}}],saturday:{id:`sat`,day:`Saturday`,sub:`Agile weekend`,classic:{name:`Lukewarm filter coffee`,note:`Has been on the hotplate since Friday, 15:00.`},veggie:{name:`Dry marble cake`,note:`Left over from the management meeting.`}}}},chantal:{page:{kind:`header`,title:`Mindful Workspace`,subtitle:`Your digital safe space for agile mindfulness.`,signoff:[`In deep connection with your KPIs,`,`Your Chantal 💕`]},older:[{title:`The Power of Silent Meetings 🤫`,time:`Posted 3 weeks ago`,paragraphs:[`Good morning, Corporate Family!`,`Our pilot project 'Silent Sync' was an enormous success. Twelve members of staff from Sales and Marketing spent an hour together in Conference Room B without exchanging a single word. We communicated purely through telepathic mind maps and energetic presence.`,`The result was breathtaking: nobody argued, there were no pointless questions, and the aura in the room was extremely agile. We are rolling the format out for all quarterly reports with immediate effect.`,`Remember: silence gives consent!`]},{title:`The Appreciation Circle 🪑`,time:`Posted 2 weeks ago`,paragraphs:[`Lovely people!`,`On Thursday we put our chairs in a circle and each of us got to tell another person what they value about them. It was very moving. A colleague from Sales cried, which I count as great progress, even though he said afterwards it had been the air conditioning.`,`For organisational reasons the circle took place during the lunch break. Appreciation should not be a drag on productivity, after all. 💫`]},{title:`Why 'No' Is Only an Unfinished 'Yes' 🌱`,time:`Posted 4 weeks ago`,paragraphs:[`Namaste, you radiant ones.`,`I have been hearing a great deal of 'no' in this building lately. 'No, that cannot be done.' 'No, there is no budget for it.' 'No, that is physically impossible.'`,`But is a no not simply a yes that is still short on enthusiasm? I invite you to go this whole week without saying no once. Watch what happens. I promise you: plenty happens.`]},{title:`Our New First-Name Culture – Compulsory from Today 🤝`,time:`Posted 6 weeks ago`,paragraphs:[`Hello lovely people — and yes, I am dropping the surnames quite deliberately!`,`From today we are on first names throughout the building. Flat hierarchies begin with language! Management is of course exempt and continues to be addressed by title and surname, so that appreciation is not watered down.`,`Anyone who finds first names difficult is welcome to come to me in confidence. I will then pass it on.`]},{title:`Digital Detox: Our Screen-Free Friday Afternoon ☀️`,time:`Posted 5 weeks ago`,paragraphs:[`You wonderful people,`,`from today, Fridays from 15:00: screens off, minds clear! We are calling it the 'Analogue Hour'. Go for a walk, draw something, breathe.`,`The handling of incoming requests is of course untouched by this. We ask you to deal with those on your mobile during the Analogue Hour. 🌞`]}],high:{title:`Here's to Our Quiet Heroes! 🙌`,time:`Posted today, 11:40`,paragraphs:[`Lovely people, something personal today for a change.`,`There is a person in this building who repairs things before we notice that they are broken. I am deliberately not saying a name, but you all know who I mean. This person did something for me today that was technical and that I did not understand, and afterwards it worked again.`,`<strong>Which is why I am proposing this to management:</strong> let us send this person a sign of appreciation. I have already set up a digital greetings card. It costs nothing and comes from the heart all the same.`,`Appreciation is the new currency! 💕`]},low:{title:`On People Who Have 'No Time' ⏳`,time:`Posted today, 11:40`,paragraphs:[`Namaste, you wonderful people.`,`I would like to talk today about a word I have come across very often of late: <em>'shortly'</em>. Some departments use this word like a piece of furniture. You stand it in the room and hope it fills the gap.`,`I am naming no names and no departments on purpose. I will say only this: understanding technology is a long way from understanding people. And anyone who does not understand people should perhaps work less with cables and more on themselves.`,`I am not angry. I am energetically disappointed. 🙏`]}},vision:{page:{kind:`interview`,badge:`Exclusive interview`,headline:`"If the ocean is a cloud, we are the windsurfing instructor."`,standfirst:`An extended conversation with our CEO, Dr Wichtig, from the current issue of 'Tech Visionary Quarterly'.`,interviewer:`Interviewer`,ceo:`Dr. Wichtig`,turns:[{q:`Dr Wichtig, your company is growing enormously. But many people are wondering: what exactly is your product? What does GlobalCorp actually make?`,a:`You know, when I was heli-skiing in the Andes the other day, standing there looking out over all that untouched snow, I thought to myself: rate of descent is really just a metaphor for Q3 revenue. We do not make 'products'. That is an analogue thought pattern from the nineteenth century! We orchestrate holistic data paradigms. We take the synergy of the blockchain, pair it with agile AI infrastructure and pour the whole thing into a scalable mindset framework.`},{q:`Honestly... I do not follow. Are you selling software? Storage?`,a:`Storage? <em>(laughs loudly)</em> We do not store data, we liberate it! We have created an ecosystem in which the user no longer consumes but transcends. Picture a doughnut. The middle is empty. That emptiness is our USP. We fill the nothing with infinite potential through machine learning. That is what our investors love so much.`},{q:`Speaking of machine learning. Everybody is talking about artificial intelligence. How does GlobalCorp integrate AI into everyday work?`,a:`For us AI is not a tool, it is a colleague. We did not programme our AI, we coached it. Last week our algorithm matrix decided to take some time out in order to focus on its core business. The server was down for two days. Now that is real machine empowerment! The competition forces its AI to work. We give ours the space to disrupt itself.`},{q:`There were reports of a massive data loss last month. Thousands of customer records turned up on the dark web.`,a:`Data loss? Please. The framing from legacy media is so exhausting. That was not a loss, that was an 'open-source data synergy event'. We freed our customers' data from its silos and gave it back to the global information ecosystem. Transparency is the new gold! Our customers ought to be thanking us that their data is now agile and decentralised across the entire world.`},{q:`And your employees? There were reports of 80-hour weeks and broken coffee machines.`,a:`My door is always open. Always. <em>(Editor's note: Dr Wichtig currently works from his yacht in the Bahamas)</em>. We are not a company here. We are an organism. If a cell in the organism has to work 80 hours, then it does so because the DNA of disruption demands it! And as for the coffee machine: we are currently evaluating a liquid-food start-up that atomises nutrients directly through the air conditioning. It saves the walk to the kitchen.`},{q:`Final question: where do you see GlobalCorp in five years?`,a:`Physical locations are so 2019. In five years we will mint our headquarters as an NFT on the Ethereum blockchain. Employees will then log in directly through their pineal gland. We will keep redefining the word 'work' until nobody knows what they are actually being paid for any more. That is absolute synergy.`}]},boss:{question:`You have a reputation as a hard negotiator. Have there been negotiations that turned out other than you had planned?`,answer:`Turned out other than planned? Negotiations do not turn out, they ripen. There was an internal conversation recently in which I gave ground on purpose, so that the person across from me could have a sense of achievement. That is what empowerment means. The fact that I signed something in the process, the terms of which my in-house solicitor read out to me afterwards, changes none of that. A good leader never loses. He delegates the victory.`},good:{question:`GlobalCorp sells state-of-the-art infrastructure. Do you actually run these technologies for your own internal processes as well?`,answer:`Naturally, we are our own reference client! Although I have to be honest: most of what runs here runs not because of the technology but because of a single member of staff in the basement. I asked him the other day how long he had been with us. He simply laughed. That kind of attachment cannot be bought. We do not even try.`},bad:{question:`GlobalCorp sells state-of-the-art infrastructure. Do you actually run these technologies for your own internal processes as well?`,answer:`Internally? <em>(pause)</em> Look, in a genuinely agile organisation technology is not a place, it is an attitude. We have an area for it in the basement, two people I believe. One? Fine. We are looking into whether that attitude could not be bought in externally at lower cost in any case. Purely strategically. There are no names on the table. There are figures.`},editorNote:`Editor's note: this interview was altered in one place after being signed off. The access came from an account with full rights. The editors could not establish which one — everybody has them.`},sales:{page:{kind:`deals`,title:`🏆 Wall of Deals`,subtitle:`Successfully closed deals. What our sales team has secured for GlobalCorp.`,leaderLabel:`Team leader`,leader:`Markus (Senior VP of Synergies)`,customerLabel:`Client:`,productLabel:`Product sold:`,deals:[{icon:`🤝`,customer:`MegaCorp Industries`,badge:`Contract signed`,tone:`signed`,product:`Predictive Blockchain Infrastructure`,rows:[{label:`Contractually guaranteed:`,text:`The system detects server failures 24 hours before they happen and repairs the hardware on its own through machine learning.`},{label:`Rollout:`,text:`End of the month. The client expects the login link on Friday.`}]},{icon:`📦`,customer:`Global Logistics`,badge:`Live`,tone:`good`,product:`Pre-Crime Delivery AI`,rows:[{label:`Contractually guaranteed:`,text:`The software knows what the end customer will order before they have even thought of it, and starts the shipping process proactively.`},{label:`Markus' note on the win:`,text:`"Told the client our algorithm reads brainwaves. We just send parcels to random addresses and call it Proactive Synergy. The board loved it!"`}]},{icon:`🛡️`,customer:`Local Bank Ltd.`,badge:`SLA active`,tone:`signed`,product:`100% Unhackable Offline Cloud Storage`,rows:[{label:`Contractually guaranteed:`,text:`The client's data is available worldwide in real time via the app, while sitting physically separated from the internet in a vacuum.`},{label:`Client note:`,text:`The bank's CIO was thrilled by Markus' concept of the 'wireless cable'.`}]},{icon:`📠`,customer:`Bundesamt für Digitalisierung`,badge:`Pilot project`,tone:`pilot`,product:`Fax-to-Blockchain Bridge`,rows:[{label:`Contractually guaranteed:`,text:`A firmware update connects the authority's conventional fax machines natively to the crypto cloud. Rubber stamps are stored as NFTs.`},{label:`Markus' note on the win:`,text:`"Easiest pitch of the year. The authority was desperate to do 'something with crypto'. We just print QR codes."`}]},{icon:`📉`,customer:`Startup XYZ`,badge:`Proof of concept`,tone:`dead`,product:`Agile Legacy Integration`,dim:!0,rows:[{label:`Contractually guaranteed:`,text:`Our cloud software is natively backwards compatible with MS-DOS 6.22.`},{label:`Status:`,text:`Awaiting sign-off. The client is still looking for a 5.25-inch floppy drive to install it from.`}]}]},good:{icon:`🔥`,customer:`Nordwind Handel KG`,badge:`Secured at the last minute`,tone:`good`,product:`Fail-Safe Real-Time Synchronisation`,rows:[{label:`Contractually guaranteed:`,text:`The client receives a permanently available connection with no maintenance window.`},{label:`Markus' note on the win:`,text:`'Client was halfway out the door, I pulled the thing out of the fire on my own. Sometimes you just need somebody who takes responsibility.'`}]},bad:{icon:`🧯`,customer:`Bremer Zulieferer GmbH`,badge:`Fallen through`,tone:`bad`,product:`Process Optimisation 360°`,rows:[{label:`Root cause analysis (Sales):`,text:`The meeting could not go ahead. The internal department responsible was unreachable during the decisive window.`},{label:`Action taken:`,text:`The matter has been passed to management for assessment. No statement from the department concerned is on file, and none was requested.`}]},phoenix:{icon:`🕳️`,customer:`Project Phoenix`,badge:`Cancelled`,tone:`dead`,product:`not ascertainable`,rows:[{label:`Contractually guaranteed:`,text:`No services are recorded in the system. No client is recorded. A budget is recorded.`},{label:`Status:`,text:`The recurring meeting in room 'Creative 2' was dissolved today. The matter stays open until somebody claims responsibility for it. It has been open for four months.`}]}},hygiene:[`The microwave in the east wing remains out of use until further notice. Somebody tried to cook frozen fish on the 'defrost' setting for 45 minutes. The smell has settled into the paint on the walls.`,`The fridge in the canteen has been defrosted. Part of the contents was older than the fridge. The remainder was not identified.`,`Whoever heats fish in the microwave is known here. Not by name. But known.`,`The jug on the hotplate is not a supply. It is a condition. Whoever empties it should please put a fresh one on.`,`The water cooler in the foyer has been disconnected. Somebody tried to plumb it straight into the coffee machine. The idea was not stupid. The execution was.`,`Leftover food does not belong in the bin under your desk. Nor in a colleague's bin. Nor in the server room.`,`The dishwasher is not a shelf. Its cycle runs for 84 minutes, not 'shortly'.`,`The toaster on the second floor has been withdrawn from service. Management has the reasoning on file. It runs to two pages.`],service:{before:{label:`Serving from 11:45`,note:`Experience shows the queue starts at 11:31.`,tone:`wait`},open:{label:`Serving now`,note:`Estimated wait according to the system: 8 minutes.`,tone:`open`},after:{label:`Serving finished`,note:`Leftovers are in the kitchenette fridge. Unlabelled. Eat at your own risk.`,tone:`closed`},done:`Already taken up today.`},impressum:{baseVersion:47,page:{kind:`sections`,title:`Legal Notice & Terms`,subtitle:`Legal advises against reading this page.`,sections:[{title:`§1 Company details`,tone:`slate`,block:[`GlobalCorp International Synergy GmbH & Co. KGaA`,`(Operations: Building 3, basement)`,`42 Tax Haven Road`,`Cayman Islands`,``,`Represented by: Dr. Wichtig (CEO & Chief Visionary Dictator)`,`Contact: If it matters, we will ring you. Not the other way round.`]},{title:`§2 Disclaimer (body & mind)`,tone:`red`,items:[`GlobalCorp accepts no liability whatsoever for any loss of sanity arising from the use of our intranet, from reading emails sent by Sales, or from eating in the canteen.`,`Spontaneous combustion of hardware manufactured after 1998 counts as an 'act of God' and is to be reimbursed by the employee privately.`,`Inhaling toner dust counts as a benefit in kind ('complimentary office make-up') and must be declared on your tax return.`,`Should an employee, through an overdose of company coffee, acquire the ability to hear colours or travel through time, any insights so obtained are the property of the company.`]},{title:`§3 Data protection & monitoring`,tone:`blue`,paragraphs:[`We take the protection of your personal data very seriously. That is why we keep it safe on our internal servers. For additional redundancy the data is backed up externally – a friendly advertising partner has generously made server capacity available for this purpose.`],lead:`By entering the company building you automatically agree that:`,items:[`Your keystrokes will be analysed to calculate your motivation (fewer than 8 keystrokes per second counts as a refusal to work).`,`Your seat cushion will collect biometric data in order to predict trips to the toilet and deduct them from your break.`,`Your DNA becomes the property of GlobalCorp the moment you lick an envelope from the company post room.`]},{title:`§4 IT resources & wear-and-tear charge`,tone:`amber`,paragraphs:[`The hardware provided at your workstation is the exclusive property of the company. We regard mouse clicks and keystrokes as finite resources. Excessive scrolling, unnecessary double-clicking or the purely private refreshing of web pages leads to premature hardware wear. From the 10,000th mouse click per calendar month, GlobalCorp reserves the right to deduct a wear charge of €0.02 per click directly from your net pay.`]}],closing:{label:`§5 Severability clause:`,text:`Should individual provisions of these terms be invalid or unenforceable, management will shout at you until you agree that they are valid after all. Place of jurisdiction is Dr Wichtig's office.`},versionLine:`Version {version}. Last amended today. {note}`},versionNote:`Separate notification of employees is not provided for.`,clauses:[{minRage:10,title:`§2c Mobile staff`,text:`Staff who have left the company premises more than ten times without signing out count as 'mobile' in employment law. Mobile staff forfeit any claim to a fixed workstation. The chair will be withdrawn during the current quarter.`},{minRage:3,title:`§2b Spontaneous changes of location`,text:`Leaving your workstation without notice counts as an unpaid break and is entered as a day of leave when the Christmas bonus is calculated. An objection may be lodged and will be archived.`}]},hr:{page:{kind:`records`,accounts:[{user:`j_schnoesel`,record:`schnoesel`},{user:`miller`,record:`mueller`}],login:{title:`Restricted Access`,subtitle:`Please authenticate in order to access personnel records.`,userLabel:`User name`,passLabel:`Password`,denied:`Access denied.`,submit:`LOG IN`},fileTitle:`Personnel record`,logout:`Log out`,sectionMaster:`Core data`,sectionDocuments:`Personal documents`,sectionBehaviour:`Behaviour & working practice`,schnoesel:{recordId:`#8472-B`,avatar:`👤`,name:`J.-A. Schnösel`,role:`Junior Agile Synergy Facilitator`,status:`Status: probation (month 1/14)`,master:[{label:`Agreed salary`,value:`€2,411.00 gross / month`,tone:`amber`,note:`(40-hour week. Plus up to 80 unpaid mandatory overtime hours per month)`},{label:`Home address`,lines:[`4 Backwoods South`,`17398 Nowhere`]},{label:`Commute`,value:`3h 15min (one way)`,tone:`red`},{label:`Holiday entitlement`,value:`14 days / year`}],documents:[{id:`motivation`,icon:`📄`,name:`CoveringLetter.pdf`,paragraphs:[`"Dear Human Capital Committee of GlobalCorp,`,`with a burning passion for cross-functional synergies and an unshakeable belief in the transformative power of agile workflows, I hereby apply for the position at your organisation.`,`My goal is to drive real disruption within your company. I want to shift outdated paradigms, break open isolated data silos and, through proactive mindset engineering, implement sustainable, scalable value chains. In my previous role (as Assistant Shift Manager at a large fast-food chain) I already proved that I can gamify complex supply-chain problems under extreme pressure.`,`I regard a private life as an unmonetised window of time. I am ready at any moment to invest my entire mental and physical capital 100% in the global mission of GlobalCorp."`]},{id:`arbeitsanweisung`,icon:`📑`,name:`Official_WorkInstruction_v4.pdf`,intro:`Confidential: core duties (level 1)`,lead:`Until further notice, the duties of the 'Junior Agile Synergy Facilitator' comprise the following manual processes:`,items:[`<strong>Coffee filter optimisation:</strong> To protect the sustainability budget, used coffee filters from the Sales department are to be dried on the radiator on the second floor, knocked out and laid ready for reuse.`,`<strong>Physical pinging:</strong> Should a colleague's Teams status in the open-plan office remain on "Away" for longer than 45 seconds, that colleague is to be visited immediately and tapped on the shoulder with a standardised wooden stick (length: 1.20m) in order to reactivate agility.`,`<strong>Plant synergy:</strong> The plastic plants in the entrance area are to be watered twice a week with tap water. This serves to maintain the illusion of an organically growing company for arriving investors.`,`<strong>Acoustic archiving:</strong> As the department head's dictaphone is broken, the employee is required to attend strategic meetings and count every spoken vowel in real time. The total is to be submitted as an Excel sheet on Fridays.`]}],notes:[{tone:`bad`,title:`Visual loss of productivity`,text:`Employee blinks on average 18 times per minute. That adds up to 2.4 working hours lost per year. An official written warning is in preparation.`},{tone:`neutral`,title:`Lack of resilience (incident 01-A)`,text:`Was found crying under the desk on his first day, after being asked to print out the internet for the weekend archive.`},{tone:`bad`,title:`Toilet inconsistency`,text:`Average time spent in the sanitary facilities is 4 minutes and 12 seconds. The GlobalCorp standard is 2 minutes and 30 seconds. From tomorrow the access code will only be issued on request.`},{tone:`good`,title:`Loyalty metric (positive)`,text:`Successfully cancelled his private streaming account in order to prepare for unpaid overtime in the evenings with greater focus. This was rewarded with a virtual high five on the intranet.`}]},mueller:{recordId:`#0404-A`,avatar:`💀`,name:`Miller`,role:`Systems administration`,statusTemplate:`Status: probation (month {month}/14)`,salaryLabel:`Agreed salary`,standbyLabel:`On-call duty`,standbyValue:`Not agreed. In practice, permanent.`,holidayLabel:`Holiday entitlement`,holidayValue:`14 days / year`,holidayNote:`(Of which 14 days are tied to the company shutdown.)`,loyaltyLabel:`Loyalty index`}},careerNotes:{warningsChef:{tone:`bad`,title:`Written warnings: {count}`,text:`All issued verbally and recorded in writing afterwards. No objection was received, as nobody was informed of the records.`},rage:{tone:`bad`,title:`Leaving the workplace without notice: {count}`,text:`The employee left the building before the end of the working day without signing out. In every case he was present again punctually the following morning, which HR notes without comment.`},ventSaves:{tone:`neutral`,title:`Programme "Mindfulness in the Cable Duct": {count} attendances`,text:`The employee has repeatedly made use of the company option to withdraw briefly before an escalation. The measure is considered effective, as no escalation followed.`},streakBest:{tone:`good`,title:`Longest run without incident: {count} working days`,text:`A conspicuously quiet period. HR is examining whether the employee was under-utilised during this time.`},survived:{tone:`good`,title:`Working days completed as scheduled: {count}`,text:`The employee left the building at the scheduled time on these days. No separate recognition is provided for, as this is what the contract requires.`}},policy:`Password policy: for reasons of system stability, IT issues the same initial password for every account. Changing it is technically possible but not provided for (Ticket #4711, open since 2019).`,support:`For technical problems please contact: miller@globalcorp.internal`,salary:`€3,150.00 gross / month`,salaryNote:`(Last adjusted in 2019. The next adjustment depends on the company targets being met.)`,loyalty:[{min:20,label:`securely attached`,text:`The employee is held in high regard across departments. A move elsewhere is unlikely, as he feels responsible for the local procedures. A salary adjustment is therefore not required.`},{min:-19,label:`unremarkable`,text:`The employee stands out neither positively nor negatively. HR records this as the ideal state.`},{min:-100,label:`flight risk elevated`,text:`There are reservations among his colleagues. As a countermeasure, a personal meeting has been scheduled. The appointment falls in the fourth quarter of 2029.`}],traitsNone:{tone:`good`,title:`Nothing to report`,text:`Nothing has been recorded in the file so far. HR reads an empty file as an indication that the employee has not been observed closely enough. A review has been initiated.`},documents:[{id:`hr_doc_stelle`,icon:`📑`,name:`JobDescription_SystemsAdministration.pdf`,intro:`Confidential: core duties (level 3)`,lead:`Until further notice, the duties of systems administration comprise every activity arising in the building that could not be allocated to any other department. In particular:`,items:[`<strong>Fault clearance:</strong> All devices with a mains connection. The demarcation from facilities is settled case by case, by shouting.`,`<strong>Support for the senior team:</strong> Availability during core hours and outside them, where the matter appears urgent. The urgency is judged by the caller.`,`<strong>Backup:</strong> Execution, verification and responsibility. No budget is provided for this, as no data loss has occurred to date.`,`<strong>Passing on knowledge:</strong> Instruction of the apprentice. Time creditable for this: none.`]},{id:`hr_doc_entwurf`,icon:`📄`,name:`ResignationLetter_DRAFT_final_v3.docx`,intro:`Last modified 14 months ago. Not sent.`,paragraphs:[`'Dear Dr Wichtig,`,`I hereby give notice to end my present employment, duly and within the notice period, with effect from'`,`<em>The sentence ends there. The document sits in the employee's personal folder and has been opened three times since, but not altered. System monitoring logs every one of those sessions and scores them positively as 'engagement with one's own future'.</em>`]}]}};export{e as intranet};